# Provider compliance

- Provider order: local extract → Google Books (with API key) → Internet Archive → Open Library.
- Without `GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY`, do not expect anonymous GB volume search to succeed (429).
- Open Library: respect rate limits; do not bulk-crawl Covers API for tens of thousands of images; prefer dumps or direct link display when required.
- Cache responses; isolate provider failures so one outage does not stop others.
- Track source, source URL, attribution, and rights_status for every cover.
- If terms only allow remote display, do not copy the image into owned storage.
- Optional providers (Hardcover, ISBNdb) are adapters — app must work when they are absent.
- Never couple the whole recovery pipeline to a single provider.
